WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:02.559
I'm sorry you're here.

2
00:00:02.559 --> 00:00:05.217
If someone you love has died,

3
00:00:05.217 --> 00:00:07.184
there's a lot to do,

4
00:00:07.184 --> 00:00:09.670
but not all of it today.

5
00:00:09.670 --> 00:00:13.100
Let's go one step at a time.

6
00:00:13.350 --> 00:00:14.681
First few days.

7
00:00:14.681 --> 00:00:18.453
Get several certified copies of the death certificate.

8
00:00:18.453 --> 00:00:21.393
The funeral home often helps order them.

9
00:00:21.393 --> 00:00:24.600
You'll need them for many accounts.

10
00:00:24.850 --> 00:00:26.127
Secure the home,

11
00:00:26.127 --> 00:00:27.631
pets, and mail.

12
00:00:27.631 --> 00:00:30.470
Let close family and key people know.

13
00:00:30.470 --> 00:00:35.100
Social Security is usually notified by the funeral home.

14
00:00:35.350 --> 00:00:37.017
Find the documents.

15
00:00:37.017 --> 00:00:38.416
Look for a will,

16
00:00:38.416 --> 00:00:40.499
trust, insurance policies,

17
00:00:40.499 --> 00:00:42.107
and account lists.

18
00:00:42.107 --> 00:00:43.744
If you find a will,

19
00:00:43.744 --> 00:00:46.095
don't change or throw it away,

20
00:00:46.095 --> 00:00:48.600
even if it looks old.

21
00:00:48.850 --> 00:00:50.432
Week one to two.

22
00:00:50.432 --> 00:00:54.175
Speak to an attorney if there's a will or trust,

23
00:00:54.175 --> 00:00:56.883
a house, or complicated family.

24
00:00:56.883 --> 00:01:00.100
Many offer a first conversation.

25
00:01:00.350 --> 00:01:02.397
Keep paying essential bills,

26
00:01:02.397 --> 00:01:04.099
like mortgage or rent,

27
00:01:04.099 --> 00:01:06.059
utilities, and insurance,

28
00:01:06.059 --> 00:01:07.616
so nothing lapses.

29
00:01:07.616 --> 00:01:11.100
Keep a log of what you pay and why.

30
00:01:11.350 --> 00:01:12.908
Week three to four.

31
00:01:12.908 --> 00:01:15.300
Ask for life insurance claim forms,

32
00:01:15.300 --> 00:01:18.900
and check retirement accounts for named beneficiaries.

33
00:01:18.900 --> 00:01:21.372
Avoid moving money out of the person's

34
00:01:21.372 --> 00:01:23.100
accounts yet.

35
00:01:23.350 --> 00:01:25.184
Don't rush big decisions.

36
00:01:25.184 --> 00:01:26.468
Selling the house,

37
00:01:26.468 --> 00:01:29.795
distributing items, or paying heirs early can create

38
00:01:29.795 --> 00:01:31.600
problems later.

39
00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:33.797
Court filings, if needed,

40
00:01:33.797 --> 00:01:36.383
usually start within weeks to months,

41
00:01:36.383 --> 00:01:38.552
and deadlines vary by state.

42
00:01:38.552 --> 00:01:42.100
A professional can tell you which apply.

43
00:01:42.300 --> 00:01:44.317
Look after yourself too.

44
00:01:44.317 --> 00:01:45.622
Ask for help.

45
00:01:45.622 --> 00:01:48.180
People usually want to.

46
00:01:48.350 --> 00:01:52.408
Our checklist keeps all of this in one place.

47
00:01:52.408 --> 00:01:54.539
And when you are ready,

48
00:01:54.539 --> 00:01:57.100
we're glad to talk.
